eated_at":"2026-10-01T23:41:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T15:59:33Z","closed_at":"2026-10-05T15:59:33Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.8-dev7\n- Not reproducible in 4.7.2 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - 4.8-dev7 - Compatibility - RX 9070 XT driver 26.9.2\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I have my Script editor open and I start the game in any other mode than the default Windowed Embedded, the Script editor grabs my keyboard input.\n\nOriginally reported as an issue in the Exclusive Fullscreen mode, but present in other modes too.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new project\n2. Change the Project Settings option Display -> Window -> Mode to `Exclusive Fullscreen` Edit: Or any mode other than Windowed, or keep the Windowed but change the run game option from embedded to floating window\n3. Attach a new script to a Node3D\n4. Open the script in the Script editor, you can paste this exit helper:\n```gdscript\nextends Node3D\n\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n\tif Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"ui_cancel\"):\n\t\tget_tree().quit()\n```\n5. Launch the game\n6. Make sure the game window/fullscreen is focused and press a key on your keyboard multiple times, e.g. <kbd>W</kbd>\n7. Exit the game by pressing <kbd>Esc</kbd>\n8. Observe a lot of W in your code\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo issue in 4.7.2 stable\n[test_4_7_2_input_fullscreen.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32937788/test_4_7_2_input_fullscreen.zip)\n\nIssue reproducible in 4.8-dev7\n[test_4_8_dev_7_input_fullscreen.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32937805/test_4_8_dev_7_input_fullscreen.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":